# NOT EXECUTABLE. Parked per BL-233: no *.feature glob and no acceptance
# runner picks this file up, so the design below is preserved without the
# runner throwing on a scenario whose step handlers do not exist yet.
#
# Why it is parked. This scenario was added to the live feature file on
# 2026-08-22 (commit 2dd75c9294) by the amendment that established the
# operation boundary. The BL-1038 parcel had already been built and
# forwarded at 6c62a65495 - it does not contain handlers for three of the
# six steps below, and the runner hard-fails on a step it cannot match.
# The BEHAVIOUR is already delivered and correct: liveRepoDerivationGuard
# requires the growth operation to target the BOUND live root by name, so a
# file's own `git init` into a temp dir is never named. What is missing is
# only the executable pinning of that boundary.
#
# Who lands it. BL-1039 - it owns repository CREATION and must show that the
# two guards do not collide on a file that performs both operations. Land it
# WITH its step handlers, in the same parcel, or leave it here.

  # BL-1038 unit-tests-pin-the-repo-they-derive-from-07
  Scenario: a test that both reads live sources and builds its own repository is flagged only for the live read
    Given a unit-lane test file that resolves the live repository root
    And that same file creates a git repository of its own
    When the guard runs
    Then the guard fails
    And the guard names the live-repository read as the violation
    And the guard does not name the created git repository as a violation
